LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T203049Z
UID:33583-1789084800-1793577599@browncountyartguild.org
SUMMARY:Founders Exhibition – Frederick W. Rigley
DESCRIPTION:September 11 – November 1\, 2026   \nThe Brown County Art Guild proudly presents the Founders Exhibition: Frederick W. Rigley\, honoring one of the Guild’s founding artists and an important figure in the development of Brown County’s artistic legacy. Drawn from private collections\, this exhibition brings together a rare selection of paintings that reflect Rigley’s deep appreciation for the landscapes\, light\, and character of southern Indiana. \nAs a founding member of the Brown County Art Guild\, Rigley helped establish an institution dedicated to preserving and promoting the artistic traditions of the region. His work captures the enduring beauty of Brown County while reflecting the values that shaped the early Guild—craftsmanship\, observation\, and a profound connection to place. \nBy gathering these seldom-seen works\, the exhibition offers visitors a unique opportunity to explore Rigley’s artistic contributions and gain a deeper understanding of the artists whose vision helped build one of Indiana’s most respected cultural organizations.
URL:https://browncountyartguild.org/event/founders-exhibition-frederick-w-rigley/
CATEGORIES:Exhibition
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncountyartguild.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/founders_exhib_web_event.jpg
END:VEVENT
