SUMMARY:Guild Speaker Series
DESCRIPTION:Rick Kelley \nBrown County Art History/Q&A\nSaturday\, September 12\n1pm – 2:30pm \nBrown County Inn  \nAs part of the 2026 Art Colony Weekend and in conjunction with the Art Colony Auction Preview\, join us for a fascinating journey into the history of one of America’s most celebrated art colonies. \nBrown County historian and resident Rick Kelley will share his deep knowledge of the Brown County Art Colony and the remarkable artists who came to these hills seeking inspiration\, community\, and a place to call home. Through engaging stories\, personal insights\, and historical anecdotes\, Rick brings the past to life\, revealing the people\, places\, and events that shaped Brown County’s rich artistic legacy. Rick will invite audience members to ask questions and share in the conversation. \nThis event is free and open to the public.
URL:https://browncountyartguild.org/event/guild-speaker-series/
CATEGORIES:Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncountyartguild.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/speakers_series_web_event.jpg
END:VEVENT
